  "lineage": "New Year's serenade of Aruba: around New Year's Eve and New Year's Day small groups go from house to house, the lead singer improvising verses that wish each household good fortune by name while the group joins the refrain, accompanied by cuatro, guitar, the wiri (metal scraper) and drum. The tradition is documented by Aruba's Instituto di Cultura; the scraper card stands in for the wiri.",
